1
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:11,820
It's a castle.

2
00:00:13,910 --> 00:00:15,880
Someone's fighting?

3
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:18,120
Strolling in through the front door would be a bad idea.

4
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:20,120
Shirou, we'll go in that way!

5
00:01:59,010 --> 00:02:03,350
{\an4}A Battle of Legend

6
00:02:22,450 --> 00:02:23,830
So that is how it is.

7
00:02:41,630 --> 00:02:44,770
Wow, that's awesome!

8
00:02:44,770 --> 00:02:47,800
No way! Those were all Noble Phantasms?

9
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:49,890
What the hell, man?

10
00:02:49,890 --> 00:02:51,770
You're crazy powerful!

11
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:56,040
Compared to that, this guy was all bark and no bite.

12
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:58,380
This is why I can't stand meat-heads!

13
00:02:57,190 --> 00:02:59,780
If you value your life, stand back, fool.

14
00:02:59,780 --> 00:03:02,410
It is far too early for laughter.

15
00:03:02,410 --> 00:03:03,640
Huh?

16
00:03:11,330 --> 00:03:15,170
I have long since grown jaded to the sight of heroes that do not fall when cut or burned.

17
00:03:15,170 --> 00:03:19,370
But I have never seen a man truly return from the dead.

18
00:03:21,250 --> 00:03:26,430
It would seem your life and legends
have taken shape as a Noble Phantasm.

19
00:03:26,430 --> 00:03:29,520
That Noble Phantasm is the one asset I lack.

20
00:03:30,070 --> 00:03:32,790
In that sense, I suppose even I stand at a disadvantage.

21
00:03:34,830 --> 00:03:39,860
Though it vexes me, it seems only the highest class of arms will work on that man.

22
00:03:43,980 --> 00:03:48,150
It is said that Heracles overcame twelve penances

23
00:03:48,150 --> 00:03:51,120
and was welcomed to the ranks of the gods afterward.

24
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:53,530
He is truly indomitable—

25
00:03:53,530 --> 00:03:55,960
the ultimate expression of human perseverance.

26
00:03:56,590 --> 00:04:00,100
My treasury, however, is the exact opposite.

27
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:03,270
It is infinite—the ultimate expression of overwhelming force.

28
00:04:03,270 --> 00:04:06,970
As you can see, it overflows with weaponry to slay heroes.

29
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:10,140
Cease playing nursemaid, Heracles.

30
00:04:10,690 --> 00:04:13,400
Fight me in earnest,

31
00:04:13,820 --> 00:04:16,730
or every last one of your labors will be for naught.

32
00:04:18,180 --> 00:04:20,900
Berserker won't lose to anyone...

33
00:04:21,610 --> 00:04:23,740
because he's the strongest in the world!

34
00:04:58,840 --> 00:04:59,990
He's back!

35
00:05:02,450 --> 00:05:03,950
Welcome back, Kiri—

36
00:05:20,510 --> 00:05:22,580
Mother?

37
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:25,830
Your mother was destroyed—

38
00:05:25,830 --> 00:05:29,510
killed at the hands of the man she loved above all others.

39
00:05:30,130 --> 00:05:32,050
What are you saying?

40
00:05:32,050 --> 00:05:34,950
Mother said that she would become the Holy Grail

41
00:05:34,950 --> 00:05:37,060
and Kiritsugu would keep her safe.

42
00:05:37,860 --> 00:05:39,750
Betrayed...

43
00:05:39,750 --> 00:05:44,910
You were... We were betrayed by that man.

44
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:49,080
And cast aside like mere tools.

45
00:05:49,380 --> 00:05:50,910
No!

46
00:05:51,660 --> 00:05:52,910
You're lying...

47
00:05:52,910 --> 00:05:53,830
You're lying!

48
00:05:53,830 --> 00:05:54,960
You must be!

49
00:05:54,960 --> 00:05:57,780
Everything you're saying must be a lie!

50
00:06:04,550 --> 00:06:06,340
Where is Kiritsugu?

51
00:06:19,780 --> 00:06:21,160
I'll be okay...

52
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:23,250
I can manage on my own.

53
00:06:23,250 --> 00:06:25,400
I'll be okay by myself.

54
00:06:31,980 --> 00:06:34,550
They say that he died.

55
00:06:34,550 --> 00:06:36,840
They say that the traitor died.

56
00:06:37,820 --> 00:06:43,460
They say he went and died, never once thinking to come back for us.

57
00:06:44,080 --> 00:06:45,600
I don't care.

58
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:47,830
That has nothing to do with me.

59
00:06:47,830 --> 00:06:50,990
I've decided to live my life by myself.

60
00:06:50,990 --> 00:06:52,890
But it has everything to do with you.

61
00:06:53,380 --> 00:06:55,440
You see, he had a child.

62
00:06:56,310 --> 00:06:59,080
That man had a family.

63
00:06:59,080 --> 00:07:01,520
A family other than me.

64
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:05,070
A family? My little brother?

65
00:07:05,840 --> 00:07:09,280
Yes. I know you'll be able to kill each other.

66
00:07:09,280 --> 00:07:11,660
You'll be able to kill each other soon.

67
00:07:11,660 --> 00:07:15,520
After all, the Greater Grail's flame was not extinguished.

68
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:20,390
The battle ended without resolution, so it will soon resume.

69
00:07:20,390 --> 00:07:22,180
I can't wait.

70
00:07:22,180 --> 00:07:25,110
I can't wait, Illyasviel!

71
00:07:25,110 --> 00:07:30,340
That gives you a reason to live, just like that human, right?

72
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:47,270
It hurts... It hurts...

73
00:07:47,270 --> 00:07:49,150
I don't want to do this anymore.

74
00:07:49,150 --> 00:07:53,250
Why does my body have to be opened up every day?

75
00:08:14,910 --> 00:08:19,500
They should just quit that stupid Holy Grail War.

76
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:21,460
We cannot.

77
00:08:21,460 --> 00:08:25,000
After all, it is our duty.

78
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,530
The miracle that occurred a thousand years ago...

79
00:08:28,100 --> 00:08:32,190
We were created in order to replicate it.

80
00:08:32,190 --> 00:08:33,850
Magic?

81
00:08:33,850 --> 00:08:35,980
Humanity's salvation?

82
00:08:35,980 --> 00:08:39,640
That will only bring happiness to humans.

83
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:42,290
What are we living for?

84
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:46,120
We have no concept of happiness,

85
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:48,210
for we are mere tools.

86
00:08:48,210 --> 00:08:50,280
We are the used, not the users.

87
00:08:50,940 --> 00:08:55,640
Even Elder Acht has probably never experienced joy.

88
00:08:55,960 --> 00:09:00,390
Yes. We are all nothing but tools to activate the Holy Grail.

89
00:09:01,020 --> 00:09:04,150
To that end, we have suffered for a thousand years.

90
00:09:04,150 --> 00:09:07,460
And then, they finally achieved you.

91
00:09:07,460 --> 00:09:10,650
Achieved me?

92
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:15,120
Yes. You are the Einzberns' crowning achievement—

93
00:09:15,120 --> 00:09:18,120
the fruit of the techniques that created us.

94
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:21,120
No matter how much time passes,

95
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:23,670
they will never be able to create one that surpasses you.

96
00:09:23,670 --> 00:09:29,200
So if you are defeated, they will all give up.

97
00:09:30,010 --> 00:09:33,430
Elder Acht will probably turn off the power source himself.

98
00:09:34,090 --> 00:09:36,350
For they will have their answer:

99
00:09:37,350 --> 00:09:40,230
that we are relics of the past.

100
00:09:40,230 --> 00:09:43,280
Everyone will give up?

101
00:09:43,280 --> 00:09:45,020
You'll all end your own lives?

102
00:09:45,530 --> 00:09:49,030
Yes, the factory known as the Einzberns

103
00:09:49,030 --> 00:09:52,330
will abandon their thousand years of research.

104
00:09:52,330 --> 00:09:53,870
With smiles on their faces,

105
00:09:53,870 --> 00:09:57,030
they will concede that they gave it their best,
but it was all for naught.

106
00:09:57,030 --> 00:09:58,610
That isn't right!

107
00:09:58,610 --> 00:10:02,480
You're all alive! Why do you have to die?

108
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:05,420
I'm the one who's gonna fight!
Shouldn't I be the one to die?!

109
00:10:06,100 --> 00:10:08,760
Do not mourn us, sweet child.

110
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:11,370
Even if everything was for nothing, we do not mind.

111
00:10:11,370 --> 00:10:12,670
Even if we cannot be saved,

112
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:17,740
we will finally be freed of our obligations.

113
00:10:21,090 --> 00:10:24,770
Duty, duty... It's always about our duty!

114
00:10:24,770 --> 00:10:26,780
Who do the Einzberns think they are?

115
00:10:26,780 --> 00:10:31,330
We never had identities of our own!

116
00:10:35,740 --> 00:10:40,850
I am Sella, and starting today, I will be looking after you.

117
00:10:40,850 --> 00:10:44,200
And this is Leysritt, who has been assigned to protect you.

118
00:10:44,720 --> 00:10:47,870
I-Illya... Nice to meet you.

119
00:10:47,870 --> 00:10:49,980
Please forgive her.

120
00:10:49,980 --> 00:10:53,030
Leysritt is still being fine-tuned—

121
00:10:53,030 --> 00:10:54,710
I don't care.

122
00:10:55,340 --> 00:10:57,860
Introductions are pointless.

123
00:10:57,860 --> 00:11:00,140
You're all the same, anyway.

124
00:11:00,550 --> 00:11:02,970
So, is the Servant here?

125
00:11:02,970 --> 00:11:06,800
Yes, the summoning has already been performed.

126
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:09,350
He is the great hero of Greek myth,

127
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:11,520
Heracles.

128
00:11:14,850 --> 00:11:16,610
How awe-inspiring.

129
00:11:16,980 --> 00:11:19,530
Rejoice, mistress!

130
00:11:19,530 --> 00:11:23,700
With a Heroic Spirit such as this, your victory is assured!

131
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:27,520
We place our lives and our meager abilities at your—

132
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:28,420
No, thank you.

133
00:11:29,140 --> 00:11:31,460
I don't need anything of the sort.

134
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:35,120
Servants are nothing more than tools.

135
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:36,970
It doesn't matter who they are.

136
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:40,140
I can manage just fine on my own.

137
00:11:40,140 --> 00:11:43,670
I'll win the Holy Grail War by myself.

138
00:11:43,670 --> 00:11:45,430
That is wrong.

139
00:11:45,940 --> 00:11:48,220
You need Berserker.

140
00:11:48,220 --> 00:11:51,940
Berserker will keep you safe.

141
00:11:52,630 --> 00:11:54,410
Don't make me laugh.

142
00:11:54,410 --> 00:11:57,900
Servants are just familiars that are bound by rules.

143
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:01,130
If not for my Command Spells, it would betray me in an instant.

144
00:12:01,130 --> 00:12:03,910
I don't trust anyone anymore.

145
00:12:04,970 --> 00:12:08,060
We will now begin linking you to Berserker.

146
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:13,130
Seventy percent of your body is composed of magic circuits,

147
00:12:13,130 --> 00:12:18,340
so you will receive far more Servant feedback than an ordinary Master.

148
00:12:18,620 --> 00:12:20,760
Please exercise the utmost caution.

149
00:12:21,310 --> 00:12:23,960
Illya, if it hurts, stop.

150
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:26,390
That doesn't matter. Let's begin.

151
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:37,230
What's going on?

152
00:12:37,660 --> 00:12:39,030
What are you doing?

153
00:12:39,030 --> 00:12:41,570
Move like I said, Berserker!

154
00:12:42,360 --> 00:12:43,660
Move, I said!

155
00:12:44,820 --> 00:12:46,640
Why won't you move?

156
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:48,570
Come on... Move!

157
00:12:48,570 --> 00:12:50,580
And you call yourself the most powerful Heroic Spirit?

158
00:12:51,090 --> 00:12:52,750
Come on, move!

159
00:13:08,710 --> 00:13:09,770
Mistress!

160
00:13:10,170 --> 00:13:11,840
Please sever the link!

161
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:14,790
Let's perform the contract ritual another time!

162
00:13:14,790 --> 00:13:17,610
This is nothing.

163
00:13:18,090 --> 00:13:21,860
I'll tame him soon enough, so be quiet and watch.

164
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:24,410
I won't be beaten.

165
00:13:24,410 --> 00:13:28,830
I'm the most powerful Master in the world!

166
00:13:56,780 --> 00:13:58,980
Huh? How did I...

167
00:13:59,470 --> 00:14:01,180
Oh, right.

168
00:14:01,180 --> 00:14:04,320
I was in the middle of the final test.

169
00:14:04,320 --> 00:14:09,460
If I make it back to the castle alive, I can go to Fuyuki.

170
00:14:09,460 --> 00:14:13,030
But I left Berserker behind.

171
00:14:13,030 --> 00:14:15,340
That's okay, though.

172
00:14:15,340 --> 00:14:19,760
When I get back to the castle, I'll just summon a new Servant.

173
00:14:22,590 --> 00:14:27,770
I'll summon one that won't cause me pain and isn't so scary.

174
00:15:01,580 --> 00:15:03,390
Berserker?

175
00:15:04,270 --> 00:15:05,900
Why are you here?

176
00:15:05,900 --> 00:15:08,680
I left you behind.

177
00:15:12,810 --> 00:15:15,300
Why aren't you fighting?

178
00:15:17,390 --> 00:15:19,230
Because of me?

179
00:15:19,850 --> 00:15:22,740
Because you don't want to make me suffer?

180
00:15:23,790 --> 00:15:25,950
Because you don't want to hurt me?

181
00:15:29,780 --> 00:15:32,710
Get them, Berserker!

182
00:15:40,150 --> 00:15:41,710
I finally understand.

183
00:15:42,540 --> 00:15:48,590
You didn't protect me because I ordered you to
or because you're a Servant.

184
00:15:49,660 --> 00:15:54,590
You've been protecting me of your own free will, haven't you?

185
00:15:56,290 --> 00:15:59,640
You're so strong, Berserker.

186
00:16:08,420 --> 00:16:09,950
He won't lose.

187
00:16:09,950 --> 00:16:13,400
Berserker won't lose to the likes of him.

188
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:14,710
Because Berserker's...

189
00:16:15,040 --> 00:16:17,120
He's stronger than anyone!

190
00:16:21,410 --> 00:16:22,840
What was that?

191
00:16:22,840 --> 00:16:24,300
Shirou...

192
00:16:25,090 --> 00:16:26,660
You understand, right?

193
00:16:26,660 --> 00:16:29,870
No matter what happens, don't get involved.

194
00:16:29,870 --> 00:16:32,770
We have no way to fight right now.

195
00:16:32,770 --> 00:16:33,900
Got it?

196
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:35,560
If you want to save people,

197
00:16:35,930 --> 00:16:38,900
save yourself first, and then think about others.

198
00:16:49,280 --> 00:16:52,300
Your defeat is certain.

199
00:16:52,300 --> 00:16:55,240
How about it? Since you will die anyway,

200
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:57,720
why not lay down your burden at the end?

201
00:16:58,770 --> 00:17:03,210
If you fight unencumbered,
you still have a chance of slaying me.

202
00:17:14,390 --> 00:17:15,980
I see.

203
00:17:16,620 --> 00:17:20,250
Then die with your mistress.

204
00:17:33,610 --> 00:17:34,990
Don't lose,

205
00:17:36,010 --> 00:17:37,160
Berserker!

206
00:17:39,190 --> 00:17:42,290
In that case, I shall impose upon you the greatest of labors!

207
00:17:47,690 --> 00:17:49,520
That makes eleven!

208
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:52,760
You're on your final life, Heracles!

209
00:18:02,190 --> 00:18:07,690
Had you forsaken your mistress at once, you would have stood a chance.

210
00:18:08,020 --> 00:18:12,240
Ultimately, were you no more than a lowly beast?
One who lived to fight?

211
00:18:12,780 --> 00:18:15,990
I had hoped for better from a fellow demigod.

212
00:18:16,260 --> 00:18:19,000
I did not take you to be such a fool.

213
00:18:33,100 --> 00:18:34,260
Berserker!

214
00:18:50,090 --> 00:18:52,170
Return to me, Berserker!

215
00:18:53,630 --> 00:18:57,950
Why? I told you to come back inside me, so why won't—

216
00:18:57,950 --> 00:18:59,500
It's no use, little puppet.

217
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:01,750
Behold the Chains of Heaven!

218
00:19:01,750 --> 00:19:06,650
None bound by these chains may escape, not even a god.

219
00:19:06,650 --> 00:19:07,420
In fact,

220
00:19:07,420 --> 00:19:11,480
those with high divinity levels such as this man
are bound all the more tightly.

221
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:16,680
Did you think I would allow you
to evacuate him via Command Spell?

222
00:19:22,990 --> 00:19:23,820
No!

223
00:19:23,820 --> 00:19:26,310
No, Berserker...

224
00:19:52,080 --> 00:19:53,320
Berserker.

225
00:19:54,130 --> 00:19:57,950
Berserker... Berserker...

226
00:20:02,390 --> 00:20:04,640
Shirou, I'm begging you!

227
00:20:10,270 --> 00:20:12,800
Huh? It hurts...

228
00:20:12,800 --> 00:20:14,160
It really hurts.

229
00:20:15,900 --> 00:20:17,540
Berserker...

230
00:20:20,310 --> 00:20:22,580
Where are you? I can't see you.

231
00:20:24,150 --> 00:20:27,580
It's all dark. I can't see anything.

232
00:20:33,400 --> 00:20:35,090
Thank goodness.

233
00:20:35,090 --> 00:20:39,150
Please stay here with me forever, Berserker.

234
00:20:54,360 --> 00:20:55,200
What?

235
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:19,810
What an unbelievable man.

236
00:21:19,810 --> 00:21:23,350
You surpassed your own myth to the very end.

237
00:21:25,020 --> 00:21:26,390
That's enough, damn it!

238
00:21:36,590 --> 00:21:40,080
Even if everything's dark, I'm not scared.

239
00:21:40,080 --> 00:21:42,460
Because you're strong, Berserker.

240
00:21:43,580 --> 00:21:47,840
With you next to me like this, I don't have to worry.

241
00:21:49,460 --> 00:21:52,680
Because you always protected me.

242
00:21:53,300 --> 00:21:56,970
You might have been scary, but actually, you were kind.

243
00:21:58,220 --> 00:22:01,850
You were big, just like a father.

244
00:22:01,850 --> 00:22:07,020
I really wanted you to scoop me up in your arms, just once.

245
00:22:14,310 --> 00:22:14,860
Yeah.

246
00:22:15,750 --> 00:22:18,740
It's kinda cold, isn't it?

247
00:23:50,650 --> 00:23:52,250
Does betrayal rub you the wrong way?

248
00:23:52,250 --> 00:23:54,410
Caster's head must be hurting, too.

249
00:23:54,410 --> 00:23:56,600
You're already messed up.

250
00:23:56,600 --> 00:23:59,090
You seem to have the will to fight, but that means nothing.

251
00:23:59,090 --> 00:24:04,380
It just pisses me off that there are Servants like you!

252
00:24:02,050 --> 00:24:04,800
A Winter's Day, the Form Wishes Take

253
00:24:02,050 --> 00:24:04,800
Next Time

